==Trivia==
*A ''[[wikipedia:Harisen|harisen]]'' is a Japanese paper fan most commonly used in [[wikipedia:Manzai|''manzai'']] comedy, in which the ''tsukkomi'' (the short-tempered "straight man" who takes things seriously) may hit the ''boke'' (the airheaded "funny man" who gets everything wrong) on the head with a ''harisen'' in response to their jokes or idiocy. The term ''tsukkomi'', also used in Harisen Cat's Japanese description, refers to when the secondary comedian "butts in" on their partner's act by reacting to, pointing out, or calling out their ridiculousness.
*This is the only cat unit in any version of [[The Battle Cats]] to change color depending on the player. In the VS and Play Together modes of [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Player 1's Mallet Cat has a red headband and mallet, which are blue for Player 2's Mallet Cat. For Harisen Cat, his tracksuit and his ''harisen''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s pivot are what change color. In single player, it will always be red.

